1
00:00:14,969 --> 00:00:17,950
WARNER BROS. PICTURES presents

2
00:00:19,974 --> 00:00:23,945
a GRIMM PICTURES and WARNER BROS. KOREA
production in association with HARBIN FILMS

3
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:28,961
a KIM JEE-WOON film

4
00:00:50,571 --> 00:00:52,380
Why do you hesitate, sir?

5
00:00:53,240 --> 00:00:55,015
I know you received the letter.

6
00:01:01,916 --> 00:01:06,189
You know how many swindlers
in this city nail up a sign,

7
00:01:06,487 --> 00:01:10,168
call themselves the "Resistance"
and come begging for cash?

8
00:01:10,827 --> 00:01:12,665
Why should I trust you?

9
00:01:16,008 --> 00:01:19,585
How can you compare us to such thieves?

10
00:01:19,867 --> 00:01:22,202
Take this thing you wanted

11
00:01:23,339 --> 00:01:25,916
and support Korea's independence.

12
00:01:32,346 --> 00:01:33,584
It's a fake.

13
00:01:34,285 --> 00:01:35,590
Is this some kind of prank?

14
00:01:35,950 --> 00:01:36,894
Sir...

15
00:01:36,895 --> 00:01:38,261
This old man is going blind!

16
00:01:39,186 --> 00:01:42,761
I was told this was a done
deal, why drag your feet?

17
00:01:48,696 --> 00:01:49,862
Then...

18
00:01:50,772 --> 00:01:53,543
why did you arrive so early?

19
00:02:40,848 --> 00:02:42,521
Listen up, Kim Jang-Ok!

20
00:02:43,117 --> 00:02:46,326
You are completely surrounded,
with no way to escape!

21
00:02:46,687 --> 00:02:48,860
Throw down your weapon and come out!

22
00:02:51,592 --> 00:02:53,128
How's it proceeding?

23
00:02:53,961 --> 00:02:55,338
He's a fierce one.

24
00:02:55,863 --> 00:02:57,296
Still holding out.

25
00:02:57,297 --> 00:03:01,177
What did you expect?
He's a core member of the Resistance.

26
00:03:18,619 --> 00:03:20,690
I'll call on him to surrender once more.

27
00:03:20,988 --> 00:03:22,023
Give me that.

28
00:03:24,024 --> 00:03:25,503
Kim Jang-Ok!

29
00:03:25,793 --> 00:03:26,863
Can you hear me?

30
00:03:27,494 --> 00:03:28,529
It's Lee Jung-Chool!

31
00:03:34,234 --> 00:03:35,907
Hold your fire! Hold your fire!

32
00:03:36,637 --> 00:03:37,637
Hold your fire!

33
00:03:45,646 --> 00:03:48,024
I'll go check the surroundings.

34
00:03:48,315 --> 00:03:50,226
Don't make a move until I return.

35
00:03:50,227 --> 00:03:51,924
Are you giving me orders?

36
00:03:53,220 --> 00:03:55,393
Why think of them as my orders?

37
00:03:55,923 --> 00:03:59,996
Chief Higashi ordered us
to capture Kim alive.

38
00:04:08,368 --> 00:04:09,369
Arrest him.

39
00:04:10,337 --> 00:04:11,372
Let's get him!

40
00:04:24,952 --> 00:04:25,952
This way!

41
00:04:36,463 --> 00:04:37,463
Don't shoot!

42
00:04:38,265 --> 00:04:39,573
I said don't shoot!

43
00:05:28,415 --> 00:05:29,415
There he is!

44
00:06:57,070 --> 00:06:58,070
Move back!

45
00:07:00,207 --> 00:07:01,207
Move back!

46
00:07:02,075 --> 00:07:03,075
Back!

47
00:07:03,677 --> 00:07:04,677
Back!

48
00:07:05,379 --> 00:07:06,414
Back!

49
00:07:07,948 --> 00:07:09,120
Everyone move back!

50
00:07:09,583 --> 00:07:10,583
Back!

51
00:07:10,951 --> 00:07:11,951
Back!

52
00:07:15,255 --> 00:07:16,757
Lee Jung-Chool...

53
00:07:32,372 --> 00:07:33,612
Jang-Ok!

54
00:07:36,209 --> 00:07:37,779
It's me, Jung-Chool.

55
00:07:38,278 --> 00:07:39,552
Let's talk it over.

56
00:07:41,548 --> 00:07:43,789
I'll open the door, so don't shoot.

57
00:08:15,248 --> 00:08:18,855
Our leaders betray the nation,
and you betray your compatriots.

58
00:08:20,020 --> 00:08:21,829
So are you living comfortably?

59
00:08:22,756 --> 00:08:24,429
Dirty traitors.

60
00:08:25,492 --> 00:08:27,972
You think we'll ever
win back independence?

61
00:08:29,863 --> 00:08:31,774
We are a sinking ship.

62
00:08:33,100 --> 00:08:34,306
Indeed.

63
00:08:35,435 --> 00:08:38,382
And rats are the first
to flee a sinking ship.

64
00:08:46,046 --> 00:08:47,218
Come out with me.

65
00:08:48,281 --> 00:08:49,954
Then you can live.

66
00:08:50,450 --> 00:08:52,555
Preserve your life at least.

67
00:08:55,989 --> 00:08:58,663
People shouldn't live among rats.

68
00:08:59,993 --> 00:09:00,993
Drop your gun!

69
00:09:02,329 --> 00:09:04,030
Long live Korea.

70
00:09:04,031 --> 00:09:05,031
Jang-Ok...

71
00:09:22,182 --> 00:09:26,494
POLICE BUREAU
OF JAPANESE HEADQUARTERS IN KOREA

72
00:09:38,165 --> 00:09:40,702
KIM JANG-OK

73
00:09:41,868 --> 00:09:43,848
<i>Deceased</i>

74
00:09:54,247 --> 00:09:55,282
Have a seat.

75
00:10:02,622 --> 00:10:04,033
It's genuine.

76
00:10:05,926 --> 00:10:08,236
They must've needed cash urgently.

77
00:10:11,932 --> 00:10:14,572
We should've captured Kim alive!

78
00:10:15,535 --> 00:10:17,742
This operation was a failure!

79
00:10:22,943 --> 00:10:24,310
Was he your friend?

80
00:10:24,311 --> 00:10:25,551
No, sir.

81
00:10:30,217 --> 00:10:31,628
Well, that's okay.

82
00:10:32,619 --> 00:10:36,260
Who can you call a friend in this age?

83
00:10:37,557 --> 00:10:41,437
Whoever offers a hand first is a friend.

84
00:10:44,297 --> 00:10:46,903
Our headquarters expects much of you!

85
00:10:48,101 --> 00:10:52,015
This figure will lead you
to the Resistance.

86
00:10:54,274 --> 00:10:55,446
We're counting on you!

87
00:11:12,692 --> 00:11:13,692
Let him go.

88
00:11:22,269 --> 00:11:27,014
SAMPANTONG RICKSHAW GARAGE
(BASE OF THE RESISTANCE)

89
00:11:27,841 --> 00:11:28,841
Where's Joo?

90
00:11:46,860 --> 00:11:50,706
After losing Jang-Ok,
they ended up only getting Joo.

91
00:11:51,031 --> 00:11:53,832
But just a day after he was caught,
Lee Jung-Chool released him.

92
00:11:53,833 --> 00:11:54,833
Lee Jung-Chool?

93
00:11:55,235 --> 00:11:57,069
The new Korean police captain.

94
00:11:57,070 --> 00:11:59,346
He worked briefly with
the Provisional Government in Shanghai.

95
00:11:59,347 --> 00:12:01,979
Then he leaked intel
to the Japanese police.

96
00:12:02,475 --> 00:12:04,887
For that, he rose
to become police captain.

97
00:12:05,178 --> 00:12:06,885
He's rotten to the core.

98
00:12:07,247 --> 00:12:09,851
He built good connections
working as an interpreter,

99
00:12:09,852 --> 00:12:11,886
but that was all just
to sell information.

100
00:12:11,887 --> 00:12:14,764
He must've released Joo as bait.

101
00:12:15,322 --> 00:12:17,890
Wait, have we been exposed?

102
00:12:17,891 --> 00:12:20,770
No, we took the long route here.

103
00:12:21,194 --> 00:12:22,229
No one followed us.

104
00:12:23,063 --> 00:12:24,542
So what do we do about Joo?

105
00:12:24,931 --> 00:12:28,105
If he won't confess
after all our pressure, it's no use.

106
00:12:28,668 --> 00:12:31,012
Just send him away.
It's not worth the effort.

107
00:12:34,441 --> 00:12:35,511
Let's do this.

108
00:12:44,718 --> 00:12:46,891
You walked out of that hell unharmed?

109
00:12:47,187 --> 00:12:50,760
I have no idea how it happened.
They told me to go, so I went.

110
00:12:51,057 --> 00:12:52,866
Lee Jung-Chool ordered you set free!

111
00:12:53,126 --> 00:12:54,693
No, comrades!

112
00:12:54,694 --> 00:12:56,970
Jang-Ok's actions
were leaked from our side!

113
00:12:57,230 --> 00:13:00,643
It's not me! It's really not me!

114
00:13:01,301 --> 00:13:05,272
Selling your compatriot
for a few coins, damn you!

115
00:13:05,538 --> 00:13:07,609
Why do you only suspect me?

116
00:13:08,908 --> 00:13:10,909
I don't know Lee Jung-Chool!

117
00:13:10,910 --> 00:13:13,891
I don't even know who he is, really!

118
00:13:18,151 --> 00:13:20,825
Only the three of us knew
about the visit that night.

119
00:13:21,121 --> 00:13:22,930
How did the police find out?

120
00:13:24,624 --> 00:13:26,160
Speak before I count to three.

121
00:13:26,593 --> 00:13:28,504
Or I'll shatter your skull.

122
00:13:29,629 --> 00:13:30,503
One.

123
00:13:30,504 --> 00:13:31,504
Who ratted on us?

124
00:13:31,831 --> 00:13:33,242
This isn't fair!

125
00:13:33,500 --> 00:13:35,907
I risked my life taking a bomb
to Central Police Station!

126
00:13:35,908 --> 00:13:37,404
How can you suspect me?

127
00:13:37,737 --> 00:13:40,411
- Two!
- Th-This is insane!

128
00:13:40,974 --> 00:13:42,783
Why only me?

129
00:13:43,310 --> 00:13:45,483
Can you all prove you aren't spies?

130
00:13:47,514 --> 00:13:49,014
C-C-C-Comrade!

131
00:13:49,015 --> 00:13:50,015
Three!

132
00:14:03,430 --> 00:14:04,430
Joo...

133
00:14:07,267 --> 00:14:09,543
Don't you know why they let you go?

134
00:14:10,503 --> 00:14:13,541
If you want to live, stay
away from both us and them.

135
00:14:21,681 --> 00:14:23,388
Leave Seoul now.

136
00:14:30,957 --> 00:14:32,129
Comrade...

137
00:14:34,394 --> 00:14:36,374
This is really hard for me.

138
00:14:43,136 --> 00:14:45,173
With their sources of cash blocked,

139
00:14:46,306 --> 00:14:49,515
the Resistance have started
selling precious objects.

140
00:14:50,810 --> 00:14:52,153
Do you know who's behind it?

141
00:14:52,812 --> 00:14:53,882
Yes, I do.

142
00:14:54,347 --> 00:14:59,558
The son of a fake painter,
an old classmate of Jo Hwe-Ryung.

143
00:14:59,919 --> 00:15:01,592
His name's Kim Woo-Jin.

144
00:15:02,188 --> 00:15:05,601
Runs a photography and antique shop
with his brother.

145
00:15:07,060 --> 00:15:09,768
People say they raise money
and send it to Shanghai.

146
00:15:10,997 --> 00:15:14,410
But why does the Resistance
suddenly need so much money?

147
00:15:15,235 --> 00:15:16,771
What are they planning?

148
00:15:17,437 --> 00:15:19,678
Might be a false rumor...

149
00:15:22,442 --> 00:15:24,683
but they're said to be buying explosives.

150
00:15:26,079 --> 00:15:28,116
According to my source in Shanghai...

151
00:15:29,048 --> 00:15:32,393
they're trying to contact
explosives experts from Hungary.

152
00:15:32,852 --> 00:15:34,525
Any news for me?

153
00:15:34,721 --> 00:15:40,569
Yes, I think I've uncovered
the Resistance's plan to raise money.

154
00:15:40,860 --> 00:15:45,741
It's led by core members
Jo Hwe-Ryung and Kim Woo-Jin

155
00:15:46,566 --> 00:15:48,978
who recently arrived in Seoul.

156
00:15:49,202 --> 00:15:51,307
Good.

157
00:15:52,539 --> 00:15:54,883
Find out if there's anyone
we can befriend.

158
00:15:55,141 --> 00:15:59,283
Introduce them to wealthy patrons,
or give them travel passes,

159
00:15:59,284 --> 00:16:02,658
since that's what they need the most.

160
00:16:02,882 --> 00:16:04,555
Yes, sir!

161
00:16:05,718 --> 00:16:07,459
From now on, you'll work with Hashimoto.

162
00:16:07,954 --> 00:16:09,399
At your service.

163
00:16:09,756 --> 00:16:11,064
I'll do my best.

164
00:16:11,791 --> 00:16:13,992
The two of us? I...

165
00:16:13,993 --> 00:16:16,803
There's nothing I won't do
to assist Captain Lee.

166
00:16:17,964 --> 00:16:20,501
I'm at your command.

167
00:16:21,134 --> 00:16:25,605
Hashimoto is pursuing Jung Che-San,
the leader of the Resistance.

168
00:16:26,072 --> 00:16:29,645
Share your intel with him.

169
00:16:30,343 --> 00:16:34,849
You two try to find some bait
that can lure Che-San.

170
00:16:36,349 --> 00:16:40,652
Your time has come
to prove your true worth.

171
00:16:40,653 --> 00:16:43,327
Captain Lee excels at this.

172
00:16:44,090 --> 00:16:46,425
Hashimoto, learn from him.

173
00:16:46,426 --> 00:16:47,496
Yes, sir!

174
00:16:52,665 --> 00:16:56,010
Have you heard of Yeon Gye-Soon
from China?

175
00:16:56,870 --> 00:17:00,317
She's a member of the Resistance
who acts as Che-San's secretary.

176
00:17:00,974 --> 00:17:04,012
She recently arrived in Seoul,

177
00:17:04,310 --> 00:17:07,018
but unfortunately, no one knows her face.

178
00:17:08,515 --> 00:17:13,692
If we catch her,
we'll have Che-San by the neck.

179
00:17:15,722 --> 00:17:18,464
YOUNGSAENG PHOTO & ANTIQUES SHOP
(SAFE HOUSE OF THE RESISTANCE)

180
00:17:27,834 --> 00:17:29,575
ls everything ready?

181
00:17:30,403 --> 00:17:34,010
Yes, you stay here. I can go myself.

182
00:17:34,641 --> 00:17:35,915
You'll go alone?

183
00:17:36,809 --> 00:17:38,254
Stay here this time.

184
00:17:39,312 --> 00:17:41,189
Wait until I deliver it.

185
00:17:42,081 --> 00:17:43,526
Things are too tense these days.

186
00:17:44,017 --> 00:17:45,017
It's dangerous.

187
00:17:45,552 --> 00:17:48,726
Are you... worried about me?

188
00:17:49,656 --> 00:17:51,693
Worried for you as a comrade.

189
00:17:53,927 --> 00:17:55,065
Comrade...

190
00:17:57,530 --> 00:18:00,568
Can you please take a photo
of your comrade?

191
00:18:01,200 --> 00:18:02,543
This is sudden.

192
00:18:03,169 --> 00:18:05,342
You've never photographed me.

193
00:18:07,340 --> 00:18:10,219
I'd like to keep it.

194
00:18:43,376 --> 00:18:45,413
One, two...

195
00:19:04,497 --> 00:19:05,771
How can I help you?

196
00:19:08,501 --> 00:19:10,174
Mr. Kim Woo-Jin?

197
00:19:10,737 --> 00:19:13,081
I'm Kim Woo-Jin.

198
00:19:16,909 --> 00:19:21,289
I've come across a precious object,
would you take a look at it?

199
00:19:25,084 --> 00:19:27,428
Yes, come upstairs.

200
00:19:44,671 --> 00:19:47,049
Do you know where it was made?

201
00:19:48,608 --> 00:19:50,281
Is it genuine?

202
00:19:56,282 --> 00:19:58,023
Let me take a look.

203
00:20:16,135 --> 00:20:18,513
You must've gone to that
cheapskate downtown.

204
00:20:19,138 --> 00:20:21,243
What a fraud he is.

205
00:20:21,841 --> 00:20:22,979
What do you mean?

206
00:20:24,677 --> 00:20:25,985
I mean it's a fake.

207
00:20:27,380 --> 00:20:30,361
Of course, only experts like me
can tell the difference.

208
00:20:32,385 --> 00:20:33,659
Really?

209
00:20:36,589 --> 00:20:38,865
I got it from a trustworthy source.

210
00:20:41,160 --> 00:20:42,764
Wait here a moment.

211
00:21:11,624 --> 00:21:13,103
Which one is genuine?

212
00:21:21,234 --> 00:21:22,611
They're exactly the same.

213
00:21:24,370 --> 00:21:27,112
One is 200 years old,
and the other one was made this spring.

214
00:21:27,774 --> 00:21:29,546
I've a pottery factory in Shanghai

215
00:21:29,547 --> 00:21:32,079
that makes antiques
out of cracked chamber pots.

216
00:21:32,945 --> 00:21:33,945
What?

217
00:21:34,480 --> 00:21:35,714
That's fraud.

218
00:21:35,715 --> 00:21:37,888
All originals have fakes.

219
00:21:38,251 --> 00:21:39,662
It's all just to meet demand.

220
00:21:40,386 --> 00:21:43,799
- You must rake in cash.
- Raking's not enough. I sweep it in.

221
00:21:44,056 --> 00:21:45,056
I'm envious.

222
00:21:45,124 --> 00:21:47,900
What work do you do
to envy a merchant like me?

223
00:21:50,163 --> 00:21:52,302
Police Bureau Captain Lee Jung-Chool.

224
00:21:55,401 --> 00:21:58,780
Forgive my rudeness!
Let me formally introduce myself.

225
00:21:59,572 --> 00:22:00,812
I'm Kim Woo-Jin.

226
00:22:01,607 --> 00:22:03,018
I didn't know who you were.

227
00:22:07,580 --> 00:22:10,527
<i>Kim Woo-Jin Shanghai Pottery Factory</i>
But what could a police captain possibly envy?

228
00:22:10,528 --> 00:22:12,792
But what could a police
captain possibly envy?

229
00:22:13,286 --> 00:22:16,290
What's so exciting
about living off a salary?

230
00:22:16,291 --> 00:22:18,963
Still, a peddler like me can't compare.

231
00:22:23,095 --> 00:22:24,095
By any chance...

232
00:22:26,032 --> 00:22:31,380
do you have connections
with the Japanese police in Shanghai?

233
00:22:31,938 --> 00:22:35,373
I could if I wanted to.
I spent time in Shanghai.

234
00:22:35,374 --> 00:22:36,785
Really?

235
00:22:37,610 --> 00:22:39,317
Then could I ask you a favor?

236
00:22:42,615 --> 00:22:45,391
I have products coming from Shanghai.

237
00:22:45,952 --> 00:22:49,124
I'm just a merchant, not some
Korean Resistance fundraiser,

238
00:22:49,125 --> 00:22:52,898
but misunderstandings block my
shipments and cause embarrassment.

239
00:22:55,394 --> 00:22:57,704
A small request like that...

240
00:22:58,698 --> 00:23:00,302
If you buy me a drink?

241
00:23:04,503 --> 00:23:08,474
Are you interested in business,
Captain Lee?

242
00:23:12,411 --> 00:23:13,913
Is it lucrative?

243
00:23:14,513 --> 00:23:19,326
How about a serious talk
about business over a drink?

244
00:23:20,419 --> 00:23:21,419
Right now?

245
00:23:21,721 --> 00:23:22,927
What do you say?

246
00:23:25,057 --> 00:23:26,057
Let's go.

247
00:23:31,430 --> 00:23:33,501
So you have quite a history.

248
00:23:37,036 --> 00:23:40,272
Jang-Ok and I are from the same hometown,

249
00:23:40,273 --> 00:23:42,844
and he and you worked together
in the Resistance,

250
00:23:42,845 --> 00:23:45,550
so you and I have a connection, as well!

251
00:23:47,346 --> 00:23:50,715
After interpreting for the Resistance,

252
00:23:50,716 --> 00:23:53,390
how'd you end up
with the Japanese police?

253
00:23:54,954 --> 00:23:57,560
You never know where life leads you.

254
00:23:58,024 --> 00:24:01,626
People are loyal to those
who look after them.

255
00:24:01,627 --> 00:24:05,871
My current chief showed a particular
interest, so I ended up there.

256
00:24:07,133 --> 00:24:12,776
It was good with Jang-Ok in Shanghai.
I thought we had a lot in common.

257
00:24:15,908 --> 00:24:18,047
I held Jang-Ok's toe in my hand.

258
00:24:21,247 --> 00:24:22,920
"It's so light."

259
00:24:23,649 --> 00:24:26,151
That's all I could think.

260
00:24:26,152 --> 00:24:28,257
Hey, I knew it.

261
00:24:29,288 --> 00:24:30,289
You...

262
00:24:31,057 --> 00:24:34,630
You're not a harsh person.
I knew from the start.

263
00:24:34,994 --> 00:24:38,441
If things had gone differently,
you'd have been a poet!

264
00:24:39,832 --> 00:24:41,243
Drink up.

265
00:24:41,968 --> 00:24:42,968
Yes.

266
00:24:43,469 --> 00:24:44,914
I will.

267
00:24:46,439 --> 00:24:48,112
I'll call you brother from now on.

268
00:24:48,841 --> 00:24:50,343
If you like.

269
00:24:50,943 --> 00:24:53,253
Whatever you want.

270
00:25:01,354 --> 00:25:02,765
Thanks for the drinks.

271
00:25:03,322 --> 00:25:04,990
Yes, yes.

272
00:25:04,991 --> 00:25:05,969
Brother...

273
00:25:05,970 --> 00:25:07,826
Thanks.

274
00:25:07,827 --> 00:25:09,135
Have a good night!

275
00:25:09,628 --> 00:25:10,766
Good-bye!

276
00:25:15,668 --> 00:25:17,170
Good night, Brother!

277
00:25:23,142 --> 00:25:24,951
TELEPHONE

278
00:26:04,517 --> 00:26:08,226
Operator, this is Police Captain
Lee Jung-Chool, get me my office.

279
00:26:13,192 --> 00:26:14,227
Sa-Hee!

280
00:26:14,560 --> 00:26:18,440
Don't come to work tomorrow,
go get the package in Sampantong.

281
00:26:22,668 --> 00:26:24,875
It's important, so be careful with it.

282
00:26:32,845 --> 00:26:36,948
<i>Japanese police are closing in.</i>

283
00:26:36,949 --> 00:26:44,189
<i>Lee Jung-Chool who worked with us
in Shanghai approached me.</i>

284
00:26:44,190 --> 00:26:52,190
<i>If our organization is exposed,
we'll regroup in Shanghai.</i>

285
00:26:56,068 --> 00:26:58,139
Contents of Captain Lee's telephone call.

286
00:27:02,108 --> 00:27:05,612
Sampantong, nine o'clock, Cacadew.

287
00:27:31,170 --> 00:27:33,844
So if the Resistance comes into Seoul,

288
00:27:34,240 --> 00:27:36,186
we can expect them
to move between these points.

289
00:27:36,175 --> 00:27:36,653
SEOUL CITY MAP

290
00:27:36,654 --> 00:27:38,849
SEOUL CITY MAP
Sacred Heart Nunnery.

291
00:27:38,850 --> 00:27:39,911
SEOUL CITY MAP

292
00:27:39,912 --> 00:27:40,786
SEOUL CITY MAP
Youngsaeng Photo Shop.

293
00:27:40,787 --> 00:27:41,787
Youngsaeng Photo Shop.

294
00:27:42,414 --> 00:27:46,624
Kim Woo-Jin, you scoundrel.
I knew it. He's their center.

295
00:27:47,286 --> 00:27:50,424
These are the movements
of the Resistance's rickshaw drivers.

296
00:27:50,425 --> 00:27:53,631
What's important is that it matches
Kim Jang-Ok's movements.

297
00:27:57,796 --> 00:27:59,332
Why has this been opened?

298
00:28:00,266 --> 00:28:02,143
Did you show it to anyone?

299
00:28:07,473 --> 00:28:08,473
Sa-Hee!

300
00:28:20,352 --> 00:28:24,389
When I left the cafe,
Captain Hashimoto was waiting.

301
00:28:24,390 --> 00:28:27,064
He said we had to share intelligence...

302
00:28:28,561 --> 00:28:29,733
Ready my car!

303
00:28:30,029 --> 00:28:31,029
Yes, sir!

304
00:28:32,865 --> 00:28:35,900
Go to the photo shop.
Before Hashimoto swoops in.

305
00:28:35,901 --> 00:28:36,901
Yes!

306
00:28:39,171 --> 00:28:40,206
Sacred Heart Nunnery.

307
00:28:48,914 --> 00:28:51,149
Excuse me, cart driver!

308
00:28:51,150 --> 00:28:52,150
Yes?

309
00:28:58,490 --> 00:29:01,926
There's a package inside,
can you load it for me?

310
00:29:01,927 --> 00:29:03,065
- Yes.
- Thanks.

311
00:29:19,845 --> 00:29:21,756
Is this the package?

312
00:29:42,935 --> 00:29:47,543
<i>The network is exposed.
Beware of Hashimoto.</i>

313
00:30:37,523 --> 00:30:39,264
I said, "Capture him alive"!

314
00:30:49,435 --> 00:30:52,109
Sister! The Japanese police
are at the gate!

315
00:30:54,340 --> 00:30:59,153
Hurry and open up!

316
00:31:17,363 --> 00:31:18,398
Be careful.

317
00:32:02,040 --> 00:32:03,040
Yes, sir!

318
00:32:04,176 --> 00:32:08,886
You idiot, you couldn't catch
even one of the girls at the nunnery?

319
00:32:09,181 --> 00:32:14,185
I said, "Keep your movements secret"!

320
00:32:14,186 --> 00:32:17,531
You call yourself a policeman
of the Great Japanese Empire?

321
00:32:20,759 --> 00:32:21,759
I'm sorry.

322
00:32:26,899 --> 00:32:28,037
Who is this?

323
00:32:28,400 --> 00:32:33,406
I-I am your i-informant.

324
00:32:36,108 --> 00:32:37,314
Captain Hashimoto...

325
00:32:38,377 --> 00:32:40,448
Chief Higashi is calling you.

326
00:33:04,102 --> 00:33:07,447
Why don't you tell the whole town...

327
00:33:08,974 --> 00:33:11,853
you're an undercover policeman?

328
00:33:15,447 --> 00:33:16,858
You useless fool...

329
00:33:20,319 --> 00:33:22,265
Take it easy, will you?

330
00:33:25,757 --> 00:33:27,168
I don't catch your meaning.

331
00:33:28,927 --> 00:33:31,134
When you're with me, speak Korean.

332
00:33:34,132 --> 00:33:39,172
I barely managed to approach them,
so why did you run wild and scare them off?

333
00:33:39,638 --> 00:33:42,278
Do we have to catch them in order?

334
00:33:42,841 --> 00:33:45,048
If they're close,
grab them before they run.

335
00:33:50,349 --> 00:33:54,820
Shouldn't you rather try to find out
how police intel was leaked?

336
00:34:02,060 --> 00:34:03,334
You are...

337
00:34:05,497 --> 00:34:07,408
challenging me, aren't you?

338
00:34:10,736 --> 00:34:13,740
We received intel
that Che-San entered Shanghai.

339
00:34:14,039 --> 00:34:16,747
He's meeting
with explosives experts there.

340
00:34:19,311 --> 00:34:20,311
Yes, sir!

341
00:34:20,846 --> 00:34:24,760
The Resistance is also streaming
out of Seoul for Shanghai.

342
00:34:25,050 --> 00:34:28,088
Antiques dealer Kim Woo-Jin
vanished this morning...

343
00:34:28,089 --> 00:34:31,022
That's because there was...

344
00:34:31,023 --> 00:34:32,195
No need to explain.

345
00:34:32,824 --> 00:34:35,059
Find him as soon as you can.

346
00:34:35,060 --> 00:34:37,540
Use all your contacts in Shanghai.

347
00:34:38,196 --> 00:34:41,700
If the Resistance is calling
explosives experts to Shanghai,

348
00:34:42,834 --> 00:34:45,212
it means they'll target
Japanese Headquarters.

349
00:34:46,171 --> 00:34:49,050
Stop the explosives from entering Seoul.

350
00:34:50,409 --> 00:34:53,049
No time to delay. Go to Shanghai at once!

351
00:34:54,446 --> 00:34:57,017
I'll offer the biggest reward
you've ever seen.

352
00:34:57,950 --> 00:35:00,931
For us, everything is in Shanghai.

353
00:35:09,962 --> 00:35:11,134
Hashimoto.

354
00:35:11,530 --> 00:35:12,530
Yes, sir?

355
00:35:47,065 --> 00:35:51,275
Stay here and report on all intel
Hashimoto sends from Shanghai.

356
00:35:51,276 --> 00:35:54,113
Report directly, not through Sa-Hee?

357
00:35:54,406 --> 00:35:56,750
Anything to do with Che-San,
report directly.

358
00:35:57,075 --> 00:35:58,520
Yes, sir.

359
00:36:03,649 --> 00:36:08,155
SHANGHAI, QINGPU DISTRICT

360
00:36:17,162 --> 00:36:18,197
I'll go.

361
00:36:35,647 --> 00:36:40,494
<i>Are you well? I'm coming
with an urgent matter to discuss.</i>

362
00:36:40,786 --> 00:36:43,995
<i>Please meet me at Shanghai Station.
Regards, Lee Jung-Chool.</i>

363
00:36:59,638 --> 00:37:02,847
We're not even safe here now.

364
00:37:03,675 --> 00:37:06,212
Why don't you wait things out
in Manchuria?

365
00:37:07,212 --> 00:37:11,524
Fighting an unknown enemy
is no simple task.

366
00:37:12,217 --> 00:37:13,821
I feel the same.

367
00:37:31,737 --> 00:37:33,717
What's Lee Jung-Chool like?

368
00:37:35,407 --> 00:37:36,909
Would he be a worthy friend?

369
00:37:39,611 --> 00:37:42,251
He and I are just bait
thrown by fishermen,

370
00:37:42,614 --> 00:37:44,423
so how could we become friends?

371
00:37:50,188 --> 00:37:52,725
Our martyr Jang-Ok spoke of him.

372
00:37:53,024 --> 00:37:54,628
Called him a close friend.

373
00:37:55,861 --> 00:37:57,135
That's all in the past.

374
00:37:59,264 --> 00:38:02,245
Right now, we lack both time and men.

375
00:38:11,076 --> 00:38:12,919
Let's take the bait.

376
00:38:19,384 --> 00:38:20,590
Turning a spy...

377
00:38:21,586 --> 00:38:24,726
We make the enemy's spy into our own.

378
00:38:26,491 --> 00:38:28,971
The most dangerous
but rewarding act of intelligence...

379
00:38:30,162 --> 00:38:32,403
is to turn a spy.

380
00:38:33,398 --> 00:38:34,399
I'm against it.

381
00:38:35,567 --> 00:38:38,104
Aren't you their ultimate target?

382
00:38:40,272 --> 00:38:41,683
Isn't it too dangerous?

383
00:38:42,607 --> 00:38:45,178
If it's in a spy's character
to switch sides...

384
00:38:47,112 --> 00:38:49,490
let's see who he stands with this time.

385
00:38:51,850 --> 00:38:54,694
Even a turncoat has only one motherland.

386
00:38:56,688 --> 00:38:58,861
Surely he feels some debt in his heart.

387
00:38:59,257 --> 00:39:00,998
We must open that up.

388
00:39:05,030 --> 00:39:09,672
There's nothing scarier
than feeling a person's emotions.

389
00:39:29,187 --> 00:39:33,033
He'll find it strange to see us
together, so you get off first.

390
00:39:48,740 --> 00:39:50,219
He's here. Smile.

391
00:39:56,848 --> 00:39:58,054
Hey, don't overdo it.

392
00:39:58,817 --> 00:40:01,485
Hey, long time no see!

393
00:40:01,486 --> 00:40:05,059
You must be busy. Great to see you!

394
00:40:41,526 --> 00:40:43,403
I looked into it as you requested.

395
00:40:44,029 --> 00:40:49,377
There are Hungarian anarchists
who know explosives and might help them.

396
00:40:50,235 --> 00:40:53,304
Some of them support Korean independence.

397
00:40:53,305 --> 00:40:54,471
Why?

398
00:40:54,472 --> 00:40:57,282
Because even with no country,
they're forming a government.

399
00:40:58,443 --> 00:40:59,643
You should see the Resistance.

400
00:41:00,478 --> 00:41:05,723
A beggar for a general,
who goes around looking for money.

401
00:41:06,718 --> 00:41:09,062
When can I meet your informant?

402
00:41:09,454 --> 00:41:11,226
After the intel was leaked in Seoul,

403
00:41:11,227 --> 00:41:13,725
the Resistance members are
nervous, so he's lying low.

404
00:41:14,926 --> 00:41:18,669
Informants are supposed to lie low,
and it's our job to find them.

405
00:41:18,670 --> 00:41:22,941
The Resistance believes we
have an informant among them.

406
00:41:25,670 --> 00:41:29,277
You're still following Lee
Jung-Chool's movements?

407
00:41:33,244 --> 00:41:35,850
Shanghai has changed a lot, too.

408
00:41:46,958 --> 00:41:48,096
I've been thinking.

409
00:41:49,127 --> 00:41:53,041
How about I quit my job and
do business here... What do you think?

410
00:41:55,600 --> 00:41:57,978
Now you've come to your senses.

411
00:41:58,269 --> 00:42:00,146
It's a splendid idea.

412
00:42:00,605 --> 00:42:03,311
Betraying your country
brings material comforts,

413
00:42:03,312 --> 00:42:05,549
but the rust in your heart is permanent.

414
00:42:05,550 --> 00:42:07,887
You talk pretty, don't you?

415
00:42:08,513 --> 00:42:13,050
Anyway, my only work here
was with the Provisional Government,

416
00:42:13,051 --> 00:42:15,895
and I've lost contact
with my old friends there.

417
00:42:16,187 --> 00:42:21,058
So I don't know anyone influential
besides the Japanese. So I'm looking for...

418
00:42:21,059 --> 00:42:22,059
Allow me...

419
00:42:22,861 --> 00:42:24,135
to finish that sentence.

420
00:42:25,497 --> 00:42:28,410
An influential Korean
close to the Provisional Government?

421
00:42:28,900 --> 00:42:31,380
How did you know before I even said it?

422
00:42:31,669 --> 00:42:34,341
You're a psychic!
Do I give away too much?

423
00:42:34,342 --> 00:42:37,684
Business is half capital,
half intuition, you know?

424
00:42:38,176 --> 00:42:40,983
Very well.
I don't know who you're seeking,

425
00:42:40,984 --> 00:42:43,391
but I'll find someone
who can connect you.

426
00:42:44,015 --> 00:42:46,552
Oh, you said you wished
to see the pottery factory?

427
00:42:46,553 --> 00:42:48,531
Let's go there now.
It's close to your hotel.

428
00:42:48,753 --> 00:42:50,323
Very good!

429
00:43:01,866 --> 00:43:02,344
FIRECRACKERS
EXPLOSIVE GUNPOWDER

430
00:43:02,544 --> 00:43:03,708
How can I help you?

431
00:43:04,341 --> 00:43:08,238
Did a foreigner buy ingredients
for explosives recently?

432
00:43:08,239 --> 00:43:10,412
We don't deal in real explosives.

433
00:43:11,709 --> 00:43:14,845
We know about your business!

434
00:43:14,846 --> 00:43:17,948
I don't know, get out!

435
00:43:17,949 --> 00:43:21,897
Wait, wait, wait! Get back here!

436
00:43:38,803 --> 00:43:41,647
She said a Hungarian rebel visits often.

437
00:43:41,973 --> 00:43:46,615
An explosives expert working in a
pharmacy in the French Concession.

438
00:43:47,312 --> 00:43:49,952
His wife is Asian.

439
00:45:08,059 --> 00:45:09,800
Let's have French cuisine tomorrow.

440
00:45:10,361 --> 00:45:12,066
How about a drink before bed?

441
00:45:12,067 --> 00:45:15,306
Tonight, sleep off your journey.
And don't forget my request.

442
00:45:15,307 --> 00:45:16,333
What?

443
00:45:16,334 --> 00:45:19,503
Remember? Getting my antiques to Seoul...

444
00:45:19,504 --> 00:45:22,007
Sure, sure!

445
00:45:25,476 --> 00:45:27,183
- Bye now!
- Good night!

446
00:45:38,356 --> 00:45:40,836
Expensive tastes, that one...

447
00:48:12,043 --> 00:48:13,043
Who's there?

448
00:49:03,528 --> 00:49:05,371
What is this at the crack of dawn?

449
00:49:06,731 --> 00:49:08,108
Let's have breakfast.

450
00:49:08,900 --> 00:49:10,038
At this hour?

451
00:49:16,974 --> 00:49:19,386
The early bird catches the worm.

452
00:49:19,877 --> 00:49:23,222
The early bird is the first to get eaten.

453
00:50:28,646 --> 00:50:30,387
Ah, bean curd stew!

454
00:50:42,293 --> 00:50:45,740
Brother, you'll have to do me a big favor.

455
00:50:47,231 --> 00:50:48,733
I told you I'd help.

456
00:50:49,534 --> 00:50:51,571
I'm risking my own neck here.

457
00:50:53,070 --> 00:50:54,674
Oh, I'm scared!

458
00:50:55,072 --> 00:50:59,987
Yes, you should be.
Your neck is at risk, too.

459
00:51:01,379 --> 00:51:03,381
For the cost of this meal?

460
00:51:21,198 --> 00:51:22,871
Is the food to your taste?

461
00:51:24,902 --> 00:51:26,108
Good to meet you.

462
00:51:27,238 --> 00:51:28,838
I'm Jung Che-San, the Resistance leader.

463
00:51:35,246 --> 00:51:38,750
I heard about you from old
Revolutionary Party comrades.

464
00:51:40,451 --> 00:51:44,092
Many of them are still thankful
for what you did, Captain Lee.

465
00:51:46,457 --> 00:51:48,403
I really wanted to meet you.

466
00:51:48,726 --> 00:51:50,899
So I asked for an introduction.

467
00:51:52,129 --> 00:51:53,129
It's an honor.

468
00:51:53,397 --> 00:51:55,274
The honor is mine.

469
00:51:55,566 --> 00:52:00,379
If not for you, how could I ever share
a meal with a Police Bureau captain?

470
00:52:02,540 --> 00:52:06,113
So how could you trust
a Police Bureau captain like me?

471
00:52:07,144 --> 00:52:09,619
Why do you glare? I didn't say anything.

472
00:52:09,620 --> 00:52:12,493
He heard of you during
your time in Shanghai.

473
00:52:13,417 --> 00:52:18,822
As compatriots sharing a meal far from
home, do we need long introductions?

474
00:52:18,823 --> 00:52:20,996
Come, let's eat.

475
00:52:22,960 --> 00:52:25,941
Oh, my. No liquor for our guest?

476
00:52:39,310 --> 00:52:41,645
Are you trying to make me rich?

477
00:52:41,646 --> 00:52:44,621
Placing me nose-to-nose
with the nation's most wanted man!

478
00:52:44,622 --> 00:52:46,322
What kind of scheme is this?

479
00:52:46,617 --> 00:52:48,290
Too young to fear anything, huh?

480
00:52:48,586 --> 00:52:51,192
I let go of my fears and my life long ago.

481
00:52:51,489 --> 00:52:53,366
Why, are you scared?

482
00:52:53,991 --> 00:52:57,438
Didn't you contact me hoping for something
like this? Now you can't handle it?

483
00:52:57,828 --> 00:53:00,206
I could kill Che-San right now.

484
00:53:00,364 --> 00:53:01,775
Give it a try.

485
00:53:02,500 --> 00:53:05,481
If I walk out of here now,
you know what'll happen?

486
00:53:06,971 --> 00:53:10,350
There'll be rumors that a police captain
and Che-San drank all night

487
00:53:10,351 --> 00:53:12,048
and became friends.

488
00:53:13,144 --> 00:53:14,623
Are you blackmailing me?

489
00:53:16,447 --> 00:53:20,054
Don't you understand
what situation you're in? Don't you?

490
00:53:21,218 --> 00:53:23,664
Has Higashi contacted you once
since arriving here?

491
00:53:29,527 --> 00:53:32,167
Why didn't that Japanese cop
tell you of his Shanghai informant?

492
00:53:32,863 --> 00:53:34,467
He wants the reward for himself.

493
00:53:35,132 --> 00:53:38,341
Playing both sides like you do
always ends in ruin.

494
00:53:53,517 --> 00:53:55,997
It's not as much as it looks.

495
00:54:00,925 --> 00:54:04,429
Come, let's drink
and talk of our hometowns.

496
00:54:06,063 --> 00:54:08,873
Contrary to his appearance,
my brother's a weak drinker.

497
00:54:10,034 --> 00:54:11,945
Since when are we brothers?

498
00:54:16,540 --> 00:54:17,540
Here.

499
00:54:19,076 --> 00:54:21,249
- Here. You, too.
- Yes, sir.

500
00:54:22,780 --> 00:54:24,282
Let's all drink.

501
00:54:31,088 --> 00:54:32,465
- Here.
- Thank you.

502
00:54:40,097 --> 00:54:42,043
Here, give me your cups.

503
00:54:47,204 --> 00:54:48,204
Here.

504
00:54:50,307 --> 00:54:51,307
Here.

505
00:54:56,247 --> 00:54:57,247
Here.

506
00:55:03,320 --> 00:55:04,320
Here.

507
00:55:16,667 --> 00:55:18,647
That didn't last long.

508
00:55:45,362 --> 00:55:46,500
Captain Lee...

509
00:55:50,801 --> 00:55:52,610
Do you like night fishing?

510
00:56:02,513 --> 00:56:06,484
Whenever I feel frustrated,
I come out here for night fishing.

511
00:56:08,285 --> 00:56:12,734
Surrounded by this cold darkness,
I forget my fears.

512
00:56:13,691 --> 00:56:15,500
You feel fear?

513
00:56:15,793 --> 00:56:16,863
Of course.

514
00:56:19,563 --> 00:56:21,167
I'm a soldier who lost his country.

515
00:56:24,668 --> 00:56:26,739
Living the meandering life of a runaway,

516
00:56:28,205 --> 00:56:30,651
the one thing I've come to master...

517
00:56:31,408 --> 00:56:33,888
is an animalistic sense for people.

518
00:56:35,646 --> 00:56:37,523
Who will come to my aid,

519
00:56:38,315 --> 00:56:40,317
who will protect my life...

520
00:56:41,218 --> 00:56:43,323
I decide it all by my instinct.

521
00:56:47,424 --> 00:56:49,836
I believed you'd help me.

522
00:56:51,095 --> 00:56:55,840
I'm just a cop on a salary,
going around chasing profit.

523
00:56:58,569 --> 00:57:00,913
I could change my mind.

524
00:57:24,695 --> 00:57:25,695
Captain Lee...

525
00:57:28,599 --> 00:57:30,806
Throw me in the ocean right now.

526
00:57:32,736 --> 00:57:34,807
If that's really what you want...

527
00:57:35,873 --> 00:57:37,147
then do it.

528
00:57:37,741 --> 00:57:39,584
This opportunity won't come again.

529
00:57:42,046 --> 00:57:44,993
How can you trust in yourself so strongly?

530
00:57:45,449 --> 00:57:49,329
I don't trust men's words.
I don't even trust my own.

531
00:57:50,287 --> 00:57:56,101
I just trust in what I must do
and what a person ought to do!

532
00:58:00,564 --> 00:58:06,105
There comes a time for everyone
to choose where to put their names.

533
00:58:07,471 --> 00:58:11,578
To which history will you
add your name, Comrade Lee?

534
00:58:30,594 --> 00:58:31,971
From now on...

535
00:58:33,130 --> 00:58:34,973
my time is in your hands.

536
00:58:44,008 --> 00:58:46,648
Help us. Can't you see we need it?

537
00:58:46,944 --> 00:58:48,044
We're desperate.

538
00:58:48,045 --> 00:58:51,618
You talk too damn much!
What do you expect of me?

539
00:58:52,182 --> 00:58:55,118
We need safe passage to Seoul. That's all.

540
00:58:55,119 --> 00:58:56,723
But there are too many obstacles.

541
00:58:57,021 --> 00:59:01,128
We'll handle what happens after.
We won't cause you trouble.

542
00:59:08,532 --> 00:59:11,172
It's your decision. I won't resent you.

543
00:59:12,803 --> 00:59:15,750
Even if I die with no grave like Jang-Ok,

544
00:59:17,074 --> 00:59:18,917
my ghost will still be loyal.

545
00:59:24,181 --> 00:59:27,253
The next time we meet,
I can't predict what I might do.

546
00:59:29,920 --> 00:59:31,058
Understand?

547
01:00:06,590 --> 01:00:08,467
It's all fake! Crazy fool tried to...

548
01:00:08,468 --> 01:00:12,236
He set up a factory, and now he's come...
now he's...

549
01:00:14,064 --> 01:00:15,236
Hey, Hashimoto!

550
01:00:19,570 --> 01:00:22,705
It's all fake. Crazy fool
tried to rip me off.

551
01:00:22,706 --> 01:00:25,619
He set up a factory, and now
he's come over to my side.

552
01:00:26,743 --> 01:00:28,482
Kim Woo-Jin is going to Tokyo.

553
01:00:28,483 --> 01:00:31,119
He wants two travel passes.
Who do you think will join him?

554
01:00:31,882 --> 01:00:33,327
Che-San, of course.

555
01:00:34,618 --> 01:00:36,085
Kim is his Number Two!

556
01:00:36,086 --> 01:00:38,999
He'll come to the pier tomorrow,
so make two travel passes!

557
01:00:40,591 --> 01:00:42,332
Is this intel accurate?

558
01:00:45,462 --> 01:00:48,170
Then I'll take the reward for myself.

559
01:00:52,736 --> 01:00:55,012
If you don't believe me, go check.

560
01:01:46,156 --> 01:01:47,567
Are you Kang Jong-Gi?

561
01:01:51,562 --> 01:01:52,836
You see anyone else here?

562
01:01:54,731 --> 01:01:56,404
Are you sure Che-San is here?

563
01:02:03,540 --> 01:02:07,420
Our goal is to take the
explosives safely to Seoul.

564
01:02:15,419 --> 01:02:18,400
They're divided among you
according to your disguises.

565
01:02:19,156 --> 01:02:20,897
The most powerful ones are in that box.

566
01:02:33,103 --> 01:02:34,103
Where'd he go?

567
01:02:35,839 --> 01:02:37,011
Damn bastards.

568
01:02:38,442 --> 01:02:42,584
Whatever happens along the way,
the boxes must reach Seoul.

569
01:02:47,417 --> 01:02:48,725
Better luck next time.

570
01:03:00,597 --> 01:03:03,203
Let's call more men to the pier tomorrow.

571
01:03:05,235 --> 01:03:06,236
Shall we go?

572
01:03:10,140 --> 01:03:12,051
After safely disembarking in Seoul,

573
01:03:12,309 --> 01:03:15,449
we'll meet one last time
at our designated rendezvous.

574
01:03:30,160 --> 01:03:33,573
Hur and I will take the boxes
to Antung Station by truck.

575
01:03:34,131 --> 01:03:37,977
From there, Hwe-Ryung
will place them in the freight car.

576
01:03:40,170 --> 01:03:46,780
So travel safely, and
let's meet in Antung.

577
01:03:56,987 --> 01:03:57,988
What's this?

578
01:03:58,922 --> 01:04:00,663
What happened here?

579
01:04:03,093 --> 01:04:04,093
Where's Kim Woo-Jin?

580
01:04:04,861 --> 01:04:07,171
We searched the pier,
but he wasn't there.

581
01:04:09,966 --> 01:04:10,966
What?

582
01:04:11,868 --> 01:04:14,041
We checked the pier,
but he wasn't there.

583
01:04:14,042 --> 01:04:15,983
How can you be so careless?

584
01:04:16,640 --> 01:04:18,449
What did your informant say?

585
01:04:19,276 --> 01:04:21,981
He doesn't know.
Too low in rank, I guess.

586
01:04:21,982 --> 01:04:25,118
So you've collected intel
from a small fish all this time?

587
01:04:25,315 --> 01:04:29,191
I have another higher up,
but I didn't want to expose him.

588
01:04:29,192 --> 01:04:32,724
Then you should have told me!
We need to move strategically!

589
01:04:33,323 --> 01:04:35,132
You think it's my decision?

590
01:04:36,560 --> 01:04:38,904
I'm just following orders from above.

591
01:04:40,697 --> 01:04:42,574
You were told to leave me out?

592
01:04:43,567 --> 01:04:44,875
On Higashi's order?

593
01:04:45,569 --> 01:04:48,743
Isn't it true there are problems
with your intel?

594
01:04:49,005 --> 01:04:50,313
Do I make up the intel?

595
01:04:50,741 --> 01:04:52,687
If your intel is shit...

596
01:04:53,710 --> 01:04:55,587
change your informants.

597
01:05:03,387 --> 01:05:05,526
Where do you spend your funds?

598
01:05:06,757 --> 01:05:07,757
What?

599
01:05:10,727 --> 01:05:13,606
I found out their route.
Not by ship, by train.

600
01:05:13,607 --> 01:05:14,701
Train?

601
01:05:15,899 --> 01:05:17,003
To where?

602
01:05:18,235 --> 01:05:21,546
They'll go separately to Antung,
then head for Seoul together.

603
01:05:21,772 --> 01:05:24,082
What? Are you sure?

604
01:05:25,442 --> 01:05:27,922
Che-San will risk his life to go to Seoul?

605
01:05:28,678 --> 01:05:29,713
Are you sure of this?

606
01:05:30,547 --> 01:05:32,948
I'm not sure if Che-San will join them.

607
01:05:32,949 --> 01:05:33,949
What?

608
01:05:34,451 --> 01:05:38,593
He's the most important,
but you don't know if he'll go or not?

609
01:05:39,556 --> 01:05:43,470
According to my source, Kim, Yeon
and the rest of them will split up,

610
01:05:43,471 --> 01:05:45,728
and then meet in Antung...

611
01:05:45,729 --> 01:05:48,801
Get out of the car
and report properly, you lout!

612
01:05:51,435 --> 01:05:52,140
What?

613
01:05:52,436 --> 01:05:54,776
Who cares if the rest of them go to Seoul?

614
01:05:54,777 --> 01:05:56,580
I'm asking where Che-San is going!

615
01:05:56,581 --> 01:05:58,307
We're not sure yet.

616
01:05:58,308 --> 01:05:59,809
Who's giving you this crappy intel?

617
01:05:59,810 --> 01:06:02,882
It's... a member of the team
traveling to Seoul.

618
01:06:02,883 --> 01:06:06,417
Wouldn't a team member know
if Che-San's going?

619
01:06:07,250 --> 01:06:10,659
No one in the Resistance knows
Che-San's route in advance.

620
01:06:10,660 --> 01:06:13,635
His course is only told
just before he departs.

621
01:06:14,324 --> 01:06:16,895
So who the hell is giving you that intel?

622
01:06:18,428 --> 01:06:20,135
That's enough. We can't tell you now.

623
01:06:20,664 --> 01:06:23,975
Okay, look into the leader's route.
We must hurry.

624
01:06:24,501 --> 01:06:26,412
What if the intel is wrong?

625
01:06:26,837 --> 01:06:29,909
If so, we'll lose all of them
and return with nothing!

626
01:06:29,910 --> 01:06:32,274
No. This time it's certain.

627
01:06:32,275 --> 01:06:34,312
This source is completely reliable.

628
01:06:34,611 --> 01:06:38,616
We promised him a big reward.
It's the person who got us Jang-Ok.

629
01:06:39,616 --> 01:06:43,496
And thanks to that source,
we're right on Che-San's heels.

630
01:06:43,854 --> 01:06:46,664
Come, we'd better hurry.

631
01:07:37,240 --> 01:07:38,741
ANTUNG STATION

632
01:07:39,187 --> 01:07:43,317
<i>The train departing for Seoul
will leave at 10 pm.</i>

633
01:07:56,593 --> 01:08:02,271
<i>The train departing for Seoul
will leave in 30 minutes.</i>

634
01:08:13,777 --> 01:08:14,777
Hey!

635
01:08:39,970 --> 01:08:45,477
<i>The train departing for Seoul
will leave in five minutes.</i>

636
01:09:12,636 --> 01:09:15,810
<i>The train departing for Seoul
will leave shortly.</i>

637
01:09:15,811 --> 01:09:19,776
<i>Please board the train promptly.</i>

638
01:09:30,020 --> 01:09:32,660
Let's split up. Who'll go where?

639
01:09:34,457 --> 01:09:38,631
Yeon and the foreigner will be in first
or second class. So I'll take her.

640
01:09:38,632 --> 01:09:41,830
So you'll arrest Yeon
and reap the glory yourself?

641
01:09:41,831 --> 01:09:42,831
What?

642
01:09:44,467 --> 01:09:47,004
Then you go that way,
I'll head to the back.

643
01:09:47,203 --> 01:09:49,376
But are they really here?

644
01:11:36,946 --> 01:11:38,714
What are you doing here?

645
01:11:38,715 --> 01:11:40,092
You've been exposed.

646
01:11:40,416 --> 01:11:41,622
Where's Yeon?

647
01:11:42,118 --> 01:11:43,722
Is she with the foreigner?

648
01:11:44,587 --> 01:11:46,567
Yes, with Ludvik in first class.

649
01:11:46,956 --> 01:11:48,492
Hashimoto went that way.

650
01:11:48,758 --> 01:11:50,897
But only our members
know about this train.

651
01:11:51,127 --> 01:11:54,301
One of your people on this train is a rat.

652
01:11:54,898 --> 01:11:56,639
The same one who sold Jang-Ok.

653
01:11:57,767 --> 01:12:00,441
I'm in danger now, too,
because of you.

654
01:12:00,670 --> 01:12:02,149
No time to talk,

655
01:12:02,438 --> 01:12:05,282
I need to find Hashimoto
and impede him somehow.

656
01:12:05,842 --> 01:12:08,345
In the meantime, think of a plan.

657
01:14:33,256 --> 01:14:36,669
<i>One of your people on this train is a rat.</i>

658
01:14:51,174 --> 01:14:52,517
Hold my bag for a second.

659
01:15:18,368 --> 01:15:19,346
No one in the back?

660
01:15:19,347 --> 01:15:21,042
No, I don't think so.

661
01:15:21,337 --> 01:15:22,543
All right.

662
01:15:28,878 --> 01:15:29,878
Hashimoto!

663
01:15:31,848 --> 01:15:33,054
Just a minute.

664
01:15:38,154 --> 01:15:39,154
Sit down here.

665
01:15:45,828 --> 01:15:49,469
If we stomp around like this,
they'll see us and change plans.

666
01:15:49,732 --> 01:15:52,178
And we have to keep them
subdued until Seoul.

667
01:15:52,179 --> 01:15:55,843
If we don't get them all,
the others might attack.

668
01:15:56,139 --> 01:16:01,143
So if you see Kim Woo-Jin
or another suspect,

669
01:16:01,144 --> 01:16:04,751
just keep an eye on them,
then grab them at the station.

670
01:16:07,316 --> 01:16:09,489
Well, you've got a point.

671
01:16:10,420 --> 01:16:11,558
Then let's do this.

672
01:16:11,854 --> 01:16:16,496
We won't be too obvious. We'll search
while moving around like passengers.

673
01:16:17,326 --> 01:16:22,097
So you mean,
you'll still search the passengers?

674
01:16:22,098 --> 01:16:23,099
Yes, of course.

675
01:16:23,566 --> 01:16:25,507
- What I meant is...
- But we'll do it quietly.

676
01:16:25,508 --> 01:16:28,572
If we don't round them up at once,
there could be trouble.

677
01:16:28,573 --> 01:16:31,609
Anyway, I'll look around.
You guys follow one car behind me.

678
01:18:11,607 --> 01:18:14,144
Sorry, I was just passing by.

679
01:18:15,344 --> 01:18:17,217
Y-You changed my baby's diaper?

680
01:18:17,218 --> 01:18:19,557
The smell is quite something. Bye, then.

681
01:18:21,951 --> 01:18:23,391
Just pretend you don't know me.

682
01:18:23,392 --> 01:18:24,660
The dining car, in 15 minutes.

683
01:18:29,458 --> 01:18:30,458
Hwe-Ryung...

684
01:18:32,461 --> 01:18:35,465
We need to change
our rendezvous in Seoul.

685
01:18:35,898 --> 01:18:37,571
I think the location's been leaked.

686
01:18:38,067 --> 01:18:40,513
Really? Where, then?

687
01:18:40,736 --> 01:18:42,738
Mokin Inn at Golden Pavilion,
four o'clock.

688
01:18:43,172 --> 01:18:46,346
Mokin Inn at Golden Pavilion,
four o'clock.

689
01:18:46,842 --> 01:18:50,813
I'll meet everyone one by one,
so don't talk needlessly.

690
01:19:08,397 --> 01:19:10,741
We need to change
our rendezvous point.

691
01:19:11,867 --> 01:19:15,280
The new place is Mokin Inn
at Golden Pavilion.

692
01:19:15,571 --> 01:19:17,414
Mokin Inn at Golden Pavilion.

693
01:19:18,341 --> 01:19:19,341
Six o'clock.

694
01:19:20,343 --> 01:19:22,289
Mokin Inn at Golden Pavilion.

695
01:19:22,612 --> 01:19:23,716
Six o'clock.

696
01:19:26,549 --> 01:19:28,119
The location has changed.

697
01:19:28,684 --> 01:19:31,358
Taehwa-banjeom, four o'clock.

698
01:19:31,587 --> 01:19:34,796
Taehwa-banjeom, four o'clock.

699
01:19:35,057 --> 01:19:38,937
Park Young-Mok's store, five o'clock.

700
01:19:39,462 --> 01:19:42,136
Don't tell anyone about this.

701
01:19:43,366 --> 01:19:44,366
All right.

702
01:20:07,089 --> 01:20:10,298
Hey! It's dangerous
to keep meeting like this!

703
01:20:11,227 --> 01:20:13,002
Listen closely.

704
01:20:13,596 --> 01:20:16,668
I told each of my members
a different rendezvous in Seoul.

705
01:20:17,833 --> 01:20:21,303
I gave them each
a different location and time.

706
01:20:22,605 --> 01:20:27,645
One of them will inform Hashimoto
before we arrive.

707
01:20:27,943 --> 01:20:30,787
That's the rat.
The one who betrayed Jang-Ok.

708
01:20:30,788 --> 01:20:32,847
But we can't keep meeting!

709
01:20:32,848 --> 01:20:36,261
Just tell me which time
and place they say.

710
01:20:36,686 --> 01:20:39,462
Why do I have to help you?

711
01:20:40,256 --> 01:20:43,260
Because if our plan is exposed,
you're in danger, too!

712
01:20:43,526 --> 01:20:46,132
In the end, you're the one
who lied to them!

713
01:20:46,762 --> 01:20:48,537
That's how we boarded this train!

714
01:20:50,366 --> 01:20:53,313
My job is to pretend
to be on your side!

715
01:20:53,469 --> 01:20:56,313
I'm the spy! Higashi approved it!

716
01:20:56,605 --> 01:20:59,484
But then you did something huge
without Higashi's knowledge.

717
01:21:00,142 --> 01:21:03,050
Every time I run into you,
you blackmail me.

718
01:21:03,051 --> 01:21:05,821
This situation leaves me no choice!
What should I do?

719
01:21:06,015 --> 01:21:07,775
Should I set off the bombs
and kill everyone?

720
01:21:09,552 --> 01:21:10,552
Brother...

721
01:21:11,287 --> 01:21:14,131
help us arrive safely, okay?

722
01:21:16,892 --> 01:21:19,736
I'll wait in the dining car. Now move!

723
01:21:24,400 --> 01:21:26,073
What an asshole!

724
01:21:31,240 --> 01:21:32,344
How did it go?

725
01:21:34,477 --> 01:21:38,012
He must be disguised,
I can't find him.

726
01:21:38,013 --> 01:21:39,487
I guess I'll keep looking.

727
01:21:39,488 --> 01:21:41,483
How about you?
Did you find your informant?

728
01:21:41,484 --> 01:21:44,055
- Not yet.
- I met the informant.

729
01:21:46,555 --> 01:21:48,034
There's a new order.

730
01:21:52,161 --> 01:21:53,936
For now, this is our plan.

731
01:21:54,230 --> 01:22:00,237
Our informant will point out
Kim Woo-Jin, Yeon and the others.

732
01:22:01,203 --> 01:22:05,379
We'll arrive at the station
without alerting them to our presence.

733
01:22:05,380 --> 01:22:11,256
Then our policemen will seal off
the station and arrest them all.

734
01:22:11,447 --> 01:22:13,948
So we won't touch them before Seoul?

735
01:22:13,949 --> 01:22:14,949
That's right.

736
01:22:15,217 --> 01:22:19,587
As you said, they outnumber us,
so it's risky to confront them.

737
01:22:19,588 --> 01:22:22,262
I think we can ride quietly
all the way to Seoul.

738
01:22:23,025 --> 01:22:26,063
Now we can sweep up the Resistance!

739
01:22:26,362 --> 01:22:29,400
And get Che-San soon, too!
This is exciting!

740
01:22:39,875 --> 01:22:42,412
I think I need a cold beer.

741
01:22:44,480 --> 01:22:46,118
Oh, will you come, too?

742
01:22:46,382 --> 01:22:49,295
No, I don't drink. You go ahead.

743
01:22:50,386 --> 01:22:54,664
We've been running around all day.
Take a rest, I'll be back soon.

744
01:23:53,048 --> 01:23:54,649
What would you like?

745
01:23:54,650 --> 01:23:56,721
- A beer.
- Yes, sir.

746
01:23:57,186 --> 01:23:58,324
I'll bring a napkin.

747
01:23:58,621 --> 01:23:59,621
Thanks.

748
01:24:11,567 --> 01:24:12,568
I'm sorry.

749
01:24:17,039 --> 01:24:18,039
Hey!

750
01:24:19,375 --> 01:24:20,479
What's with you?

751
01:24:21,644 --> 01:24:22,679
Don't worry about it.

752
01:24:23,145 --> 01:24:24,145
Hey!

753
01:24:25,247 --> 01:24:27,193
It's okay. Don't worry. Let's sit.

754
01:24:29,251 --> 01:24:30,662
Are you sure?

755
01:24:56,278 --> 01:24:57,279
Hey...

756
01:24:58,414 --> 01:25:00,951
I thought something happened to you.

757
01:25:01,951 --> 01:25:04,124
I went out for some air.

758
01:25:04,553 --> 01:25:05,554
Did you hear?

759
01:25:06,055 --> 01:25:07,055
Yes.

760
01:25:08,257 --> 01:25:09,736
Where and what time?

761
01:25:11,961 --> 01:25:17,240
Mokin Inn at Golden Pavilion.

762
01:25:20,636 --> 01:25:22,445
<i>Mokin Inn at Golden Pavilion.</i>

763
01:25:23,072 --> 01:25:24,072
Four o'clock.

764
01:25:27,543 --> 01:25:28,647
<i>Four o'clock.</i>

765
01:25:33,248 --> 01:25:37,390
Don't be reckless.
Make trouble, and we all die!

766
01:25:37,886 --> 01:25:40,264
You work things out yourselves.
Don't ever contact me...

767
01:25:45,060 --> 01:25:46,835
Hey, Woo-Jin...

768
01:25:47,830 --> 01:25:49,571
I think we've reached the end.

769
01:25:59,575 --> 01:26:01,282
Didn't you say you'd stay?

770
01:26:02,745 --> 01:26:05,316
Well, after thinking it over,

771
01:26:07,650 --> 01:26:10,351
I thought I'd share a beer
with you after all.

772
01:26:10,352 --> 01:26:11,352
One beer.

773
01:26:11,587 --> 01:26:12,587
Yes, sir.

774
01:27:10,145 --> 01:27:12,056
That tea smells nice.

775
01:27:18,554 --> 01:27:21,160
Have you got anything to say to me?

776
01:27:25,661 --> 01:27:30,041
He looks awfully similar to the guy
we're looking for, right?

777
01:27:38,707 --> 01:27:39,845
What are you talking about?

778
01:27:39,846 --> 01:27:44,018
I'll take command now. Think straight!

779
01:27:45,547 --> 01:27:48,790
I will command and you will follow.

780
01:27:55,758 --> 01:27:57,601
Police. Show me identification.

781
01:28:05,067 --> 01:28:06,375
Wait, don't move!

782
01:28:07,302 --> 01:28:08,372
Hey!

783
01:28:21,583 --> 01:28:23,961
My ID is in the bag, take it if you wish.

784
01:28:25,621 --> 01:28:29,091
Both of you listen.
One slip and we all die.

785
01:28:30,092 --> 01:28:35,667
That depends on who subdues
the other first. Think it over.

786
01:28:45,841 --> 01:28:46,945
Kim Woo-Jin.

787
01:29:04,827 --> 01:29:05,827
Now!

788
01:29:52,474 --> 01:29:55,318
You damned traitor!

789
01:30:08,991 --> 01:30:10,024
Out of the way!

790
01:30:10,025 --> 01:30:11,265
Move! Out of the way!

791
01:30:15,197 --> 01:30:19,737
Damn fool had a death wish.

792
01:30:20,102 --> 01:30:21,445
Step aside, it's dangerous!

793
01:30:26,575 --> 01:30:28,577
I'm a Captain of the
Japanese Police Bureau.

794
01:30:29,077 --> 01:30:32,524
I'm performing my duties,
so return to your places quietly.

795
01:30:32,781 --> 01:30:33,781
Yes, sir!

796
01:30:52,067 --> 01:30:53,205
A change of heart?

797
01:31:01,743 --> 01:31:03,916
More like a hardened heart.

798
01:31:05,113 --> 01:31:07,150
I lost my faith in this a while back.

799
01:31:08,550 --> 01:31:10,418
My heart's no longer in it.

800
01:31:10,419 --> 01:31:14,265
You talk like we're a store
going bankrupt.

801
01:31:14,756 --> 01:31:17,464
If we had just one success,
I wouldn't be this way.

802
01:31:18,160 --> 01:31:21,266
Getting country hicks
to throw bombs for independence...

803
01:31:24,066 --> 01:31:25,841
I can't play dumb anymore.

804
01:31:28,437 --> 01:31:30,075
No use in going to Seoul.

805
01:31:30,772 --> 01:31:33,480
It's hopeless.
Even if I do you this favor.

806
01:31:33,481 --> 01:31:36,979
Favor? Who? To whom? You to me? To us?

807
01:31:40,015 --> 01:31:41,517
If not for me...

808
01:31:43,118 --> 01:31:44,995
you'd all have been exposed.

809
01:31:45,520 --> 01:31:46,999
But you're my friend.

810
01:31:47,622 --> 01:31:49,465
You're all like family!

811
01:31:50,859 --> 01:31:52,497
Shouldn't you be grateful?

812
01:31:57,165 --> 01:31:58,974
This is vengeance for Jang-Ok.

813
01:32:18,887 --> 01:32:23,063
You're not really going to let
this foreigner kill me, are you?

814
01:32:24,626 --> 01:32:28,506
In the name of the Resistance,
you are executed for spying.

815
01:32:35,303 --> 01:32:36,304
Woo-Jin!

816
01:32:37,539 --> 01:32:38,984
See you in hell.

817
01:32:50,719 --> 01:32:53,359
Once we arrive, I don't know you.

818
01:32:57,259 --> 01:32:58,259
Take this with you.

819
01:33:04,032 --> 01:33:06,774
If we meet again, one of us dies.

820
01:33:07,936 --> 01:33:09,244
Or both of us.

821
01:34:32,954 --> 01:34:38,802
GYEONGSEONG STATION, SEOUL

822
01:34:41,496 --> 01:34:43,498
SEOUL STATION

823
01:35:44,326 --> 01:35:45,326
Go.

824
01:35:47,195 --> 01:35:48,196
Show me the pass.

825
01:35:53,068 --> 01:35:54,068
Next.

826
01:35:56,071 --> 01:35:57,106
Passport.

827
01:35:59,507 --> 01:36:00,507
Next.

828
01:36:08,116 --> 01:36:09,186
The pass.

829
01:36:29,404 --> 01:36:30,404
Ludvik.

830
01:36:33,775 --> 01:36:34,810
Everyone come!

831
01:36:37,979 --> 01:36:38,979
Go!

832
01:36:44,886 --> 01:36:45,886
Yeon Gye-Soon!

833
01:37:03,405 --> 01:37:04,405
Run!

834
01:37:11,446 --> 01:37:12,446
There!

835
01:37:48,550 --> 01:37:49,550
Hey!

836
01:38:38,400 --> 01:38:39,936
Calm down!

837
01:38:40,702 --> 01:38:41,935
Calm down, calm down!

838
01:38:41,936 --> 01:38:42,846
Let go!!

839
01:38:42,847 --> 01:38:43,941
Captain Kim Woo-Jin!

840
01:39:46,601 --> 01:39:47,671
My apologies.

841
01:39:49,337 --> 01:39:50,577
How do you feel?

842
01:39:52,607 --> 01:39:54,177
I'll recover quickly.

843
01:39:59,080 --> 01:40:03,028
After being shot and falling off
a train, your condition is...

844
01:40:03,451 --> 01:40:05,362
a relief.

845
01:40:10,024 --> 01:40:12,800
The loss of Hashimoto is lamentable...

846
01:40:16,297 --> 01:40:20,439
but you deserve much credit.

847
01:40:35,016 --> 01:40:39,192
We recovered prime bait
for catching the big fish.

848
01:40:46,127 --> 01:40:47,538
Can you guess who?

849
01:41:05,246 --> 01:41:09,422
You're multilingual, but surely
most comfortable in Korean.

850
01:41:10,985 --> 01:41:14,831
Now we have someone to ask you in Korean.

851
01:41:16,758 --> 01:41:19,739
Ask Kim Woo-Jin's whereabouts.

852
01:41:24,365 --> 01:41:25,571
Where is Kim Woo-Jin?

853
01:41:28,736 --> 01:41:29,736
Wait.

854
01:41:34,275 --> 01:41:35,845
That won't do.

855
01:42:03,571 --> 01:42:04,879
Kim Woo-Jin...

856
01:42:05,907 --> 01:42:07,944
Just tell us where he is.

857
01:42:09,744 --> 01:42:10,984
I don't know.

858
01:42:11,746 --> 01:42:14,886
I don't know anything.

859
01:42:30,665 --> 01:42:32,008
Captain Lee!

860
01:42:40,008 --> 01:42:41,008
Chief...

861
01:42:42,510 --> 01:42:43,614
Do it.

862
01:42:45,813 --> 01:42:46,813
Do it!

863
01:42:58,092 --> 01:43:00,038
You just need to tell us!

864
01:43:00,361 --> 01:43:01,795
Come on and tell us!

865
01:43:01,796 --> 01:43:02,499
I don't know!

866
01:43:02,500 --> 01:43:03,498
- Tell us!
- I don't!

867
01:43:03,499 --> 01:43:06,633
- Tell us!
- I really don't know! No!

868
01:43:06,634 --> 01:43:09,012
- I said tell us!
- Don't do it!

869
01:43:09,303 --> 01:43:11,112
Please tell us! Please!

870
01:43:39,233 --> 01:43:45,047
KOREA BRANCH MILITARY POLICE HEADQUARTERS

871
01:43:47,508 --> 01:43:49,510
You look upset.

872
01:43:51,179 --> 01:43:53,159
No, sir.

873
01:43:54,182 --> 01:43:57,391
I heard you two were close in Shanghai.

874
01:43:59,153 --> 01:44:01,724
Do you suspect me?

875
01:44:13,601 --> 01:44:18,414
Other people suspected you
from the start, but not me.

876
01:44:20,108 --> 01:44:25,683
And due to the nature of your work,
during an operation...

877
01:44:26,748 --> 01:44:30,252
I don't ask too many questions.

878
01:44:33,121 --> 01:44:36,034
Governor-General Terauchi
said at his inauguration,

879
01:44:37,058 --> 01:44:44,806
"Koreans can choose to obey
Japanese rule, or die."

880
01:44:46,467 --> 01:44:49,573
It's your lot in life to be born Korean.

881
01:44:51,606 --> 01:44:53,244
So whatever you may have done,

882
01:44:55,376 --> 01:44:56,912
I'll forget everything.

883
01:45:00,214 --> 01:45:02,421
Just bring me Kim Woo-Jin.

884
01:45:36,617 --> 01:45:37,617
Let's just go.

885
01:45:53,835 --> 01:45:55,109
Seo Jin-Dol!

886
01:45:59,540 --> 01:46:00,678
Seo Jin-Dol!

887
01:46:01,142 --> 01:46:04,851
Oh, my, when will this weather let up?

888
01:46:12,854 --> 01:46:13,958
Drag him in.

889
01:46:16,023 --> 01:46:17,468
You're deported!

890
01:46:24,465 --> 01:46:26,843
It's the police! Run, quick!

891
01:46:40,314 --> 01:46:43,727
Mother, I need to go far away.
You must live!

892
01:46:58,099 --> 01:47:00,010
Mother, you must live!

893
01:47:00,935 --> 01:47:02,005
Let go!!

894
01:47:02,703 --> 01:47:03,703
Mother!

895
01:47:45,246 --> 01:47:46,919
Aren't you going home?

896
01:49:03,724 --> 01:49:04,998
Hey, Joo!

897
01:49:17,705 --> 01:49:20,413
Woo-Jin visited Jeongneung House.

898
01:49:21,909 --> 01:49:24,981
He said to ask you to make him an ID.

899
01:49:26,547 --> 01:49:27,890
He said you'd help him.

900
01:50:11,058 --> 01:50:12,058
Kim Woo-Jin!

901
01:50:17,364 --> 01:50:18,741
What happened to everyone?

902
01:50:23,404 --> 01:50:25,384
It'll be hard for Yeon to hold out.

903
01:50:27,374 --> 01:50:29,149
It serves you right.

904
01:50:29,577 --> 01:50:31,386
For being so cocky.

905
01:50:33,247 --> 01:50:34,419
You must leave.

906
01:50:35,282 --> 01:50:39,321
A coal ship for Japan...
If you leave now, you can catch it.

907
01:50:41,989 --> 01:50:43,229
How is my brother?

908
01:50:44,458 --> 01:50:45,664
I haven't seen him.

909
01:50:47,828 --> 01:50:49,102
Then why are you here?

910
01:50:49,763 --> 01:50:50,798
Because of Joo.

911
01:50:52,133 --> 01:50:53,133
Joo?

912
01:50:53,767 --> 01:50:56,145
You told him to find me for an ID.

913
01:51:30,704 --> 01:51:32,183
That way! Hurry! Hurry!

914
01:51:40,981 --> 01:51:42,016
Take him alive!

915
01:51:45,686 --> 01:51:47,029
Shoot his leg!

916
01:52:01,635 --> 01:52:02,635
Kim Woo-Jin!

917
01:52:08,042 --> 01:52:09,544
Lee Jung-Chool got away.

918
01:52:09,843 --> 01:52:10,878
What?

919
01:52:17,384 --> 01:52:18,658
Kim Woo-Jin...

920
01:52:20,154 --> 01:52:23,033
Surely you didn't trust Lee Jung-Chool.

921
01:52:25,059 --> 01:52:27,505
He's the one who turned you in.

922
01:52:30,764 --> 01:52:32,266
Where are the explosives?

923
01:52:33,367 --> 01:52:35,745
Right under your nose.

924
01:52:37,771 --> 01:52:39,876
I guess we've been too gentle.

925
01:52:40,774 --> 01:52:43,721
You still have some spirit.

926
01:52:44,845 --> 01:52:48,019
However long it takes,
you'll tell us eventually.

927
01:52:49,750 --> 01:52:51,752
That's not going to happen.

928
01:52:53,020 --> 01:52:54,693
Ever.

929
01:53:01,595 --> 01:53:05,805
Was Yeon your lover?

930
01:53:18,912 --> 01:53:21,153
Want to hear a funny story?

931
01:53:23,050 --> 01:53:27,658
You all think you were caught
because of your rat?

932
01:53:28,422 --> 01:53:33,895
We didn't know Yeon's face, but
we caught her because of her photograph.

933
01:53:36,597 --> 01:53:38,338
The one you took at your studio.

934
01:53:48,575 --> 01:53:52,182
Let's see how much you can take.

935
01:53:54,415 --> 01:53:55,860
You dreadful man.

936
01:53:56,784 --> 01:53:57,784
Begin.

937
01:54:19,673 --> 01:54:21,016
He bit his tongue!

938
01:54:23,711 --> 01:54:25,782
You still haven't found the explosives?

939
01:54:27,781 --> 01:54:30,022
Chief! We caught Lee Jung-Chool.

940
01:55:41,388 --> 01:55:42,423
All rise!

941
01:55:54,768 --> 01:55:55,768
Please be seated.

942
01:55:59,773 --> 01:56:01,480
The court is now in session.

943
01:56:08,615 --> 01:56:10,891
We will hear the defendant's statement.

944
01:56:16,290 --> 01:56:18,133
Lee Jung-Chool.

945
01:56:19,226 --> 01:56:20,296
Lee Jung-Chool!

946
01:56:21,562 --> 01:56:22,563
Come forward.

947
01:56:44,685 --> 01:56:45,789
Please begin.

948
01:56:47,754 --> 01:56:52,362
I planned to accept the explosives
from Kim Woo-Jin and confiscate them,

949
01:56:52,363 --> 01:56:54,669
so I didn't report in advance.

950
01:56:56,196 --> 01:56:58,870
I waited for the remaining
Resistance members

951
01:56:59,666 --> 01:57:02,476
and intended to arrest them all at once.

952
01:57:18,185 --> 01:57:22,793
As a police official,
I tried to fulfill my mission.

953
01:57:24,725 --> 01:57:30,334
And believing that success
could get me a promotion,

954
01:57:32,666 --> 01:57:35,806
I infiltrated the enemy.

955
01:57:40,040 --> 01:57:41,212
I...

956
01:57:54,755 --> 01:57:59,704
As a Japanese policeman...

957
01:58:01,995 --> 01:58:04,339
I merely tried my best.

958
01:58:07,534 --> 01:58:12,040
I'm not a member of the Resistance.

959
01:58:13,840 --> 01:58:16,218
I only intended to use Kim Woo-Jin.

960
01:58:20,747 --> 01:58:24,854
I'm not his comrade nor his friend!

961
01:58:39,733 --> 01:58:42,475
This is so unfair!

962
01:59:04,324 --> 01:59:06,065
The dog of Japan is here!

963
01:59:07,160 --> 01:59:09,663
I'll be watching you!

964
01:59:09,997 --> 01:59:11,908
Because of you, I'm here forever!

965
01:59:11,909 --> 01:59:13,065
Filthy traitor!

966
01:59:13,066 --> 01:59:15,801
I'm going to beat you to a pulp!

967
01:59:15,802 --> 01:59:17,782
Hey, Lee Jung-Chool!

968
01:59:18,405 --> 01:59:22,285
ONE MONTH LATER

969
01:59:39,826 --> 01:59:41,328
Hey, silent guy...

970
01:59:43,997 --> 01:59:48,173
Yeon died this morning.

971
02:00:48,228 --> 02:00:50,333
Why is it so small?

972
02:00:52,899 --> 02:00:54,708
She starved herself to death.

973
02:00:56,703 --> 02:01:00,412
She came from China, and had
no friends or relatives.

974
02:01:04,111 --> 02:01:08,560
No good place to bury her,
but I can't throw her away.

975
02:01:31,772 --> 02:01:34,309
I'm in a hurry. Please step aside.

976
02:01:34,808 --> 02:01:35,809
Step aside.

977
02:02:28,295 --> 02:02:31,833
You haven't eaten a bite. No appetite?

978
02:02:43,143 --> 02:02:44,383
Are you going somewhere?

979
02:02:48,381 --> 02:02:49,792
Chief Higashi?

980
02:02:50,550 --> 02:02:52,621
<i>He has a banquet to attend,.</i>

981
02:02:52,886 --> 02:02:56,493
<i>A charity event at the Police Bureau Club,.</i>

982
02:02:57,624 --> 02:02:59,331
Who will come to the event?

983
02:02:59,793 --> 02:03:02,695
<i>High-ranking police bureaucrats,</i>

984
02:03:02,696 --> 02:03:06,667
<i>imperial Parliament members
and supporters of the regime.</i>

985
02:03:42,569 --> 02:03:43,569
Brother...

986
02:03:47,774 --> 02:03:49,048
Brother...

987
02:03:52,512 --> 02:03:53,957
You take the explosives.

988
02:03:55,081 --> 02:03:57,956
While I go out and distract them,
you hide them.

989
02:03:57,957 --> 02:03:59,222
You're crazy to the end.

990
02:03:59,223 --> 02:04:00,721
And promise one more thing.

991
02:04:02,088 --> 02:04:05,729
Even if you're caught, hold out
to the end. Say you're not part of us.

992
02:04:07,294 --> 02:04:08,898
Because one of us has to live.

993
02:04:09,195 --> 02:04:12,438
So the operation will succeed.
So our lives won't be wasted!

994
02:04:17,904 --> 02:04:18,905
Thanks for everything.

995
02:04:19,873 --> 02:04:21,784
I never could've made it without you.

996
02:05:12,993 --> 02:05:18,773
JAPAN AND KOREA UNITE
NIGHT OF NATIVE KOREANS

997
02:07:37,670 --> 02:07:39,911
Ladies and gentlemen,
Bureau Chief Higashi!

998
02:08:14,874 --> 02:08:15,874
Cheers!

999
02:08:16,142 --> 02:08:17,382
Cheers!

1000
02:08:34,561 --> 02:08:35,562
Let's go.

1001
02:09:16,269 --> 02:09:19,682
<i>Deceased</i>

1002
02:10:14,327 --> 02:10:18,002
Officer! Officer! Are the rumors true?

1003
02:10:18,298 --> 02:10:19,777
Quiet, you!

1004
02:10:29,075 --> 02:10:30,076
Hey!

1005
02:10:30,510 --> 02:10:32,421
Hey, silent guy!

1006
02:10:33,680 --> 02:10:35,091
Did you hear?

1007
02:10:38,851 --> 02:10:41,195
An explosion at the Police Bureau Club

1008
02:10:41,854 --> 02:10:44,528
killed and injured many people.

1009
02:10:46,292 --> 02:10:47,669
It's chaos.

1010
02:10:48,328 --> 02:10:50,137
They've never seen such a hell.

1011
02:10:51,497 --> 02:10:58,437
But they still haven't found half
of the Resistance's explosives.

1012
02:11:01,774 --> 02:11:04,118
That's even scarier.

1013
02:11:48,721 --> 02:11:52,168
Well, it's better than letting
the Japanese grab it.

1014
02:11:54,026 --> 02:11:58,600
But promise. If people know my money
is going to the fighters, it's a problem.

1015
02:11:58,898 --> 02:12:01,071
Keep it a secret until independence.

1016
02:12:02,034 --> 02:12:04,412
You think independence will come, sir?

1017
02:12:06,906 --> 02:12:08,943
With guys like you, I'm sure it will.

1018
02:12:11,077 --> 02:12:12,077
Sir...

1019
02:12:13,713 --> 02:12:15,454
and how much for this?

1020
02:12:18,951 --> 02:12:24,128
There are more Government Medals
in this city than scoundrels.

1021
02:12:28,795 --> 02:12:31,969
How much do I owe you?

1022
02:12:32,598 --> 02:12:35,579
The amount you received
for betraying Kim Jang-Ok.

1023
02:12:41,607 --> 02:12:43,109
Who said that?

1024
02:12:43,409 --> 02:12:45,082
Jo Hwe-Ryung? Joo?

1025
02:13:42,001 --> 02:13:43,674
Take this, too.

1026
02:13:52,378 --> 02:13:53,823
I'll succeed for sure.

1027
02:13:55,147 --> 02:13:56,888
Is Che-San well?

1028
02:13:57,316 --> 02:13:59,353
Yes, he's fine.

1029
02:14:00,353 --> 02:14:05,200
He cried bitterly during
the hearing about your operation.

1030
02:14:06,492 --> 02:14:08,472
Then he said this...

1031
02:14:09,228 --> 02:14:11,469
"Even when we fail, we move forward.

1032
02:14:12,665 --> 02:14:18,513
The failures accrue, and we tread anthem
to advance to higher ground."

1033
02:14:26,045 --> 02:14:29,720
Do you have any message to pass on to him?

1034
02:14:38,691 --> 02:14:40,068
"See you again."

1035
02:15:16,729 --> 02:15:20,199
<i>"Even when we fail, we move forward."</i>

1036
02:15:20,800 --> 02:15:23,871
<i>The failures accrue, and we tread on them
to advance to higher ground."</i>

1037
02:15:23,872 --> 02:15:28,443
JAPANESE HEADQUARTERS IN KOREA
<i>The failures accrue, and we tread on them to advance to higher ground."</i>

1038
02:16:03,275 --> 02:16:14,975
<i>Resistance fighters pass through here.</i>
